# README for < English -> Chinese Simplified tranlation >, by Liu Xuan, 2014.10
# （1）Prepositions in English such as 'from' & 'of', are a bit difficult to translate when a whole sentence is sliced into pieces.
#      e.g. 'Playing track from Internet' is easy to transalte into '正在从互联网播放音轨'，but 'Playing track from' will be
#           incomplete in Chinese. Current solution is '正在从此处播放音频：'（notice the Full-width colon added in the end!）；
#      e.g. ‘out of' -> '/'.
# （2）One word might be translated into different Chinese words according to the context.
#      e.g. peer -> 伙伴 or 伙伴用户; authorize -> 允许 or 授权； track -> 音轨 or 曲目
# （3）Some translations are comprehensible, but not perfect yet. They are listed as belows(perhaps you have better ideas):
#      Handpicked -> 自选的，Discard -> 丢弃，Review -> 审阅（Previous translation: 检视）
# END of README
